-- ============================================================================
-- 022 — Real building footprints from OpenStreetMap (map geometry)
--
-- SOURCE:    OpenStreetMap via the Overpass API
--            https://overpass-api.de/api/interpreter
--            Query: way|relation["building"](around:700,-37.7964,144.9631)
-- RETRIEVED: 2026-08-15
-- LICENCE:   Building geometry (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL 1.0.
--            https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright
--            Attribution is required wherever this geometry is redistributed,
--            including in this repository. See README.
--
-- ── What was wrong ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
--
-- Every building on the map was a quadrilateral. Migration 010 replaced the
-- original oversized rectangles, and 011 replaced those with what it called
-- "OSM actual outline" — but 011's shapes were hand-simplified to 4-7 points,
-- so a courtyard building like Old Arts was a flat four-cornered slab. No
-- version of this database has ever held a real footprint.
--
-- These are the actual OSM ways, unsimplified: 14 to 57 vertices each.
--
-- ── And some were in the wrong place ────────────────────────────────────────
--
-- Matching was done by NAME against OSM, not by proximity, precisely because
-- some seeded coordinates are wrong and proximity matching inherits the error.
-- Melbourne School of Design was seeded at 144.95810 — beside Baillieu, on the
-- west of campus. It occupies the Glyn Davis Building on Masson Road, 428 m
-- east. Centroids are recomputed from the footprint, so position now derives
-- from the geometry rather than being asserted alongside it.
--
-- ── Not covered ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
--
-- Three buildings are deliberately left untouched, because they could not be
-- identified in OSM with any confidence and guessing would reintroduce exactly
-- the error this migration removes:
--
--   engineering-1   Seed 001 calls it "Engineering Building 1 (Block B)", a
--                   name UoM does not publish. OSM has Infrastructure
--                   Engineering Blocks B/C/D, Mechanical, and two Chemical
--                   Engineering buildings. No basis to choose between them.
--   ict-building    No OSM feature by this name. The ICT Building at 111 Barry
--                   Street was superseded by Melbourne Connect; whether this
--                   record means the old building or the new one is unclear.
--   kwong-lee-dow   No OSM feature by this name anywhere within 700 m.
--
-- Two buildings exist in OSM as multiple ways and only the larger is used:
-- Chemistry (West Wing, East Wing is way/1151933132) and David Caro (North
-- Wing, South is way/23024009). A single Polygon column cannot hold both.
-- ============================================================================

